        "id": "p133-q73-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that if $P(x)$ is an odd function, then the coefficients of all even powers of $x$ must be zero.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p133-q73-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a_k=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for every even index ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0\\le k\\le n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", including ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a_0=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p133-q73-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Compare coefficients of even powers in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(-x)=-P(x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-x)&=a_0+a_1(-x)+a_2(-x)^2+\\cdots+a_n(-x)^n\\\\P(-x)&=a_0-a_1x+a_2x^2-\\cdots+(-1)^n a_nx^n.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $P$ is odd, for every real $x$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-x)&=-P(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing coefficients of $x^k$ for each even index $k$ with $0\\le k\\le n$ gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a_k&=-a_k\\\\2a_k&=0\\\\a_k&=0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus every even-power coefficient, including the constant coefficient $a_0$, is zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p133-q73-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Prove that if $P(x)$ is an even function, then the coefficients of all odd powers of $x$ must be zero.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
